# Universal contract: desk source files are UTF-8, LF. PowerShell tools that
# write UTF-16/CRLF into this tree must be banned (breaks every brain's hash
# verification). Normalize on add/checkout so any CRLF working copy is visible
# in git status as a diff, not silently stored.
*.py    text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.jsonl text eol=lf
*.ps1   text eol=crlf
# BOX STATE AT THE DESK ROOT, COMMITTED WITH CRLF (2026-10-06). These seven are
# libs/ops/release.py STATE_FILES paths, so their content is the box's and is never rewritten on
# origin -- not even to renormalise it. Each blob holds CRLF (the Dell hourly sync, 2026-08-17),
# and under the *.json eol=lf rule above such a blob can never match a checkout, so every clone
# showed all seven modified. -text stores them byte-for-byte: a CRLF write from the box is not
# dirty, and nothing is rewritten. Exact paths only: the live copies under data/ and reports/
# stay eol=lf, and their writers pin newline="\n". Pinned by tests/test_sync_marker_is_written_lf.py.
/sync_marker.json -text
/gateway_state.json -text
/hunt11.json -text
/mech_battery.json -text
/mech_split.json -text
/portfolio_projection.json -text
/regime_state.json -text
